1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,588
Here is a peptide chain.

2
00:00:01,588 --> 00:00:05,950
Twenty letters to choose from, and this one has its own exact order.

3
00:00:05,950 --> 00:00:07,369
Change just one link.

4
00:00:07,369 --> 00:00:09,427
Not the whole chain, just one.

5
00:00:09,427 --> 00:00:10,742
It is not a typo.

6
00:00:10,742 --> 00:00:12,265
It is not close enough.

7
00:00:12,265 --> 00:00:15,143
It is a different molecule, with a different name.

8
00:00:15,143 --> 00:00:18,476
One letter swapped, and everything downstream changes.

9
00:00:18,476 --> 00:00:21,041
That is how sensitive the order really is.

10
00:00:21,041 --> 00:00:22,968
Follow for more peptide math.

